Generic PIDE bridge
===================

Keep MCP.bridge/MCP.bridge_result, the versioned envelope, independent call IDs,
theory-local operation registry and one executor. Each call freshly resolves the
configured root theory. Retained built-in operations are tools, run_tool and
check_context; descendant theories may register further operations.

Keep hello readiness validation against the reduced required operation set,
request admission, one terminal owner, cancellation, deadlines, correlated errors,
worker groups, shutdown drain acknowledgement and bounded fallback session stop.
Keep existing reply byte protection and output isolation. Request-byte enforcement
is a pre-existing missing boundary and remains explicitly deferred. ML tool results retain structured XML bodies.

Tool declaration notifications remain independent fan-out events and are tested
while operations are pending. The root supplies the catalogue and selected tool;
target resolution stays in ML and does not select a different implementation.

Retain deterministic operation-correlation and lifecycle tests plus real bridge
checks on Pure and HOL registration foundations. Refresh the payload measurement
corpus for retained operations; previous measurements of removed operations are
not current verification. Run all declared layers before closing this plan.

Request-byte disposition (approved 2026-09-10)
---------------------------------------------
The inspected baseline has no maxRequestBytes guard in the Scala send path or
ML request decoder. The user explicitly chose to preserve actual baseline
protections and not restore this missing feature during the carve-out. Former
pide_bridge#T11 is retired from this cut with that deferred reason, not passed,
waived as implemented, or attributed to the carve-out. Request payload corpus
measurements do not establish enforcement. Reply limits and admission/lifecycle
protections remain active acceptance obligations.

Live root ownership (approved 2026-09-10)
---------------------------------------
The server owns one live PIDE document root from startup through shutdown.
Bootstrap loads it before hello and readiness requires successful final end.
The root is always a private temporary wrapper importing exactly the selected
-T theory through PIDE, whether image or source. Its context supplies the catalogue
and default execution. Reprocess ancestors and wrapper for updates. Keep
its document requirement alive for the server lifetime. Every call selects the
current successful document root; there is no heap lookup fallback. Shutdown
drains bridge work, then releases the document requirement and stops the session.
Every internal hello/call carries mandatory root_node, root_command and root_exec
attributes alongside the existing theory identity. The node names the owned
wrapper; command and evaluation IDs select its completed final end. Use existing
Isabelle snapshot/Document APIs only, with no prover-source patches. ML checks
current execution identity, completion, final-end state and theory identity before
selecting the root. Missing, malformed, stale or unfinished selectors fail through
correlated errors, without fallback or automatic retry. Replies, cancel/drain,
operation payloads and public context arguments remain unchanged.
Do not reject unrelated document edits through global snapshot quiescence checks.
Compare the selected wrapper evaluation against the current ML document execution.
An admitted call retains its resolved immutable theory; later calls select again.
